IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- sga-part1.l4: Part 1 (sections 1 to 5C) of the Superannuation Guarantee (Administration) Act 1992 (Commonwealth),
-- Federal Register compilation C2026C00272, plain-text conversion (not the authorised text).
-- Section 1 (short title), section 2 (commencement) and section 4 (extent) are machinery and are not encoded as rules; NOTES.md says so.
-- A function answers JUST FALSE only where the text says no in its own words; otherwise NOTHING (the text does not say).

§ `Section 3: the Act binds the Crown`

DECLARE Government IS ONE OF
    `the Commonwealth`
    `a State`
    `the Australian Capital Territory`
    `the Northern Territory`
    `a government not named in section 3`

-- src:30 | (1) This Act binds the Crown in right of the Commonwealth, each State, the Australian Capital Territory and the Northern Territory.
@ref s 3(1) (src:30-30)
GIVEN government IS A Government
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`this Act binds the Crown in right of` MEANS
    CONSIDER government
    WHEN `the Commonwealth` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a State` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `the Australian Capital Territory` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `the Northern Territory` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a government not named in section 3` THEN NOTHING

-- "Nothing in this Act permits ...": a flat negative.
-- src:31 | (2) Nothing in this Act permits the Crown to be prosecuted for an offence.
@ref s 3(2) (src:31-31)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`this Act permits the Crown to be prosecuted for an offence` MEANS JUST FALSE

§ `Section 5: the Commonwealth, its Departments and untaxable authorities`

DECLARE `Body` IS ONE OF
    `the Commonwealth`
    `a Commonwealth Department`
    `an untaxable Commonwealth authority`
    `any other person`

-- src:35 | (1) The Commonwealth, Commonwealth Departments and untaxable Commonwealth authorities are not liable to pay superannuation guarantee charge.
@ref s 5(1) (src:35-35)
GIVEN body IS A `Body`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`section 5(1) makes the body liable to pay superannuation guarantee charge` MEANS
    CONSIDER body
    WHEN `the Commonwealth` THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN `a Commonwealth Department` THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN `an untaxable Commonwealth authority` THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN `any other person` THEN NOTHING

-- 5(4): the listed provisions of the Taxation Administration Act 1953 "do not apply" to those three bodies.
-- src:47 | (4) Subsection 14ZX(4), section 14ZZ and Divisions 4 and 5 of Part IVC of the Taxation Administration Act 1953 do not apply to the Commonwealth, Commonwealth Departments or untaxable Commonwealth authorities.
@ref s 5(4) (src:47-47)
GIVEN body IS A `Body`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`subsection 14ZX(4), section 14ZZ and Divisions 4 and 5 of Part IVC of the Taxation Administration Act 1953 apply to the body` MEANS
    CONSIDER body
    WHEN `the Commonwealth` THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN `a Commonwealth Department` THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN `an untaxable Commonwealth authority` THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN `any other person` THEN NOTHING


-- 5(5) "Commonwealth Department": (a) to (c) are alternatives; the person states which, if any, applies.
-- src:49 | Commonwealth Department means:
-- src:50 | (a) a Department of State; or
-- src:51 | (b) a Department of the Parliament established under the Parliamentary Service Act 1999; or
-- src:52 | (c) a branch or part of the Australian Public Service in relation to which a person has, under an Act, the powers of, or exercisable by, the Secretary of a Department of the Australian Public Service.
@ref s 5(5) "Commonwealth Department" (src:49-52)
GIVEN `a Department of State` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a Department of the Parliament established under the Parliamentary Service Act 1999` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a branch or part of the Australian Public Service whose Secretary-like powers are held by a person under an Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`is a Commonwealth Department` MEANS
        `a Department of State`
    OR `a Department of the Parliament established under the Parliamentary Service Act 1999`
    OR `a branch or part of the Australian Public Service whose Secretary-like powers are held by a person under an Act`

-- src:53 | Commonwealth entity means a Commonwealth entity (within the meaning of the Public Governance, Performance and Accountability Act 2013) that cannot be made liable to taxation by a Commonwealth law.
@ref s 5(5) "Commonwealth entity" (src:53-53)
GIVEN `a Commonwealth entity within the meaning of the Public Governance, Performance and Accountability Act 2013` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a Commonwealth law can make it liable to taxation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`is a Commonwealth entity for section 5` MEANS
        `a Commonwealth entity within the meaning of the Public Governance, Performance and Accountability Act 2013`
    AND NOT (`a Commonwealth law can make it liable to taxation`)

-- src:62 | untaxable Commonwealth authority means an authority of the Commonwealth that cannot, by a law of the Commonwealth, be made liable to taxation by the Commonwealth.
@ref s 5(5) "untaxable Commonwealth authority" (src:62-62)
GIVEN `an authority of the Commonwealth` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a law of the Commonwealth can make it liable to taxation by the Commonwealth` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`is an untaxable Commonwealth authority` MEANS
        `an authority of the Commonwealth`
    AND NOT (`a law of the Commonwealth can make it liable to taxation by the Commonwealth`)

-- 5(5) "responsible Department": where the remuneration is or was paid wholly or principally out of money appropriated ...
DECLARE `Source of remuneration` IS ONE OF
    `an annual Appropriation Act`
    `an Act other than an annual Appropriation Act, and the employee performs or performed the duties in or in respect of a Commonwealth Department`
    `an Act other than an annual Appropriation Act, in any other case`
    `the Constitution`

DECLARE `Responsible Department` IS ONE OF
    `the Commonwealth Department in respect of which the money was appropriated`
    `the Commonwealth Department in or in respect of which the duties are performed`
    `the Department of State administered by the Minister who administers the Act under which the money was appropriated`
    `the Finance Department`

-- src:56 | responsible Department, in relation to the employment of a Commonwealth employee, means:
-- src:57 | (a) where the remuneration in respect of that employment is or was paid wholly or principally out of money appropriated under an annual Appropriation Act—the Commonwealth Department in respect of which the money was appropriated; and
-- src:58 | (b) where the remuneration in respect of that employment is or was paid wholly or principally out of money appropriated under an Act other than an annual Appropriation Act:
-- src:59 | (i) if the employee performs or performed the duties of that employment in, or in respect of, a Commonwealth Department—that Commonwealth Department; or
-- src:60 | (ii) in any other case—the Department of State administered by the Minister who administers the Act under which that money was appropriated, insofar as the Act appropriated that money; and
-- src:61 | (c) where the remuneration in respect of that employment is or was paid wholly or principally out of money appropriated by the Constitution—the Finance Department.
@ref s 5(5) "responsible Department" (src:56-61)
GIVEN source IS A `Source of remuneration`
GIVETH A `Responsible Department`
`the responsible Department` MEANS
    CONSIDER source
    WHEN `an annual Appropriation Act` THEN `the Commonwealth Department in respect of which the money was appropriated`
    WHEN `an Act other than an annual Appropriation Act, and the employee performs or performed the duties in or in respect of a Commonwealth Department` THEN `the Commonwealth Department in or in respect of which the duties are performed`
    WHEN `an Act other than an annual Appropriation Act, in any other case` THEN `the Department of State administered by the Minister who administers the Act under which the money was appropriated`
    WHEN `the Constitution` THEN `the Finance Department`

-- 5(3): charge of a responsible Department or untaxable authority is treated as paid on the day it would have become payable had the entity been a company.
-- src:43 | (3) Part 8 has effect as if any superannuation guarantee charge in respect of a superannuation guarantee shortfall of either of the following entities:
-- src:44 | (a) a responsible Department;
-- src:45 | (b) an untaxable Commonwealth authority;
-- src:46 | had been paid on the day that the charge would have become payable had that entity been a company.
@ref s 5(3) (src:43-46)
GIVEN `the day the charge would have become payable had the entity been a company` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the day the charge of a responsible Department or untaxable Commonwealth authority is treated as paid` MEANS
    `the day the charge would have become payable had the entity been a company`

-- 5(2B), 5(2C): a direction of the Finance Minister that is in writing and is necessary or convenient to give effect to section 5 has effect and must be complied with.
-- src:41 | (2B) The Finance Minister may give such directions in writing as are necessary or convenient to be given for carrying out or giving effect to this section and, in particular, may give directions in relation to the transfer of money within an account, or between accounts, operated by the Commonwealth or a Commonwealth entity.
-- src:42 | (2C) Directions under subsection (2B) have effect, and must be complied with, notwithstanding any other law of the Commonwealth.
@ref s 5(2B), (2C) (src:41-42)
GIVEN `the direction is in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the direction is necessary or convenient for carrying out or giving effect to section 5` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`a direction of the Finance Minister has effect and must be complied with` MEANS
    IF `the direction is in writing` AND `the direction is necessary or convenient for carrying out or giving effect to section 5`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- 5(2), 5(2A): the Act applies "as if" the employee were employed by the responsible Department, the responsible Department were a company, each other Department and
-- authority were a company related to it, and the responsible Department were a government body; modifications may be prescribed.
-- src:36 | (2) However, subject to this Act and to such modifications as are prescribed, this Act applies in all other respects, in respect of any matter or thing in respect of the employment of a Commonwealth employee, as if:
-- src:37 | (a) the employee were employed by the responsible Department and not by the Commonwealth; and
-- src:38 | (b) the responsible Department were a company and each other Department, and each authority of the Commonwealth, were a company related to the responsible Department; and
-- src:39 | (c) the responsible Department were a government body.
-- src:40 | (2A) In addition, subject to such modifications as are prescribed, this Act applies in relation to an untaxable Commonwealth authority in the same way as it applies in relation to a Commonwealth Department.
@ref s 5(2), (2A) (src:36-40)
GIVEN `the employee is a Commonwealth employee` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the Act treats the responsible Department as the employer and as a company and a government body` MEANS
    IF `the employee is a Commonwealth employee` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

§ `Section 5A: Commonwealth authorities`

-- src:64 | (1) In this section:
-- src:65 | Commonwealth authority means an authority or body that is established by or under a law of the Commonwealth.
@ref s 5A(1) (src:64-65)
GIVEN `established by or under a law of the Commonwealth` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`is a Commonwealth authority` MEANS `established by or under a law of the Commonwealth`

-- 5A(2) and (3): whether the exemption, apart from this section, would apply to the charge; when the law was passed; whether it expressly exempts from the charge.
-- src:66 | (2) If:
-- src:67 | (a) a law, or a provision of a law, passed before the commencement of this section purports to exempt a Commonwealth authority from liability to pay:
-- src:68 | (i) taxes under the laws of the Commonwealth; or
-- src:69 | (ii) certain taxes under the laws of the Commonwealth; and
-- src:70 | (b) apart from this subsection, the exemption would apply to superannuation guarantee charge;
-- src:71 | that law or provision is taken not to have exempted, or not to exempt, that authority from liability to pay the charge.
@ref s 5A(2), (3) (src:66-71)
-- src:72 | (3) If:
-- src:73 | (a) a law, or a provision of a law, passed after the commencement of this section purports to exempt a Commonwealth authority from liability to pay:
-- src:74 | (i) taxes under the laws of the Commonwealth; or
-- src:75 | (ii) certain taxes under the laws of the Commonwealth; and
-- src:76 | (b) apart from this subsection, the exemption would apply to superannuation guarantee charge;
-- src:77 | the law or provision is not taken to have exempted, or to exempt, the authority from liability to pay the charge unless the law or provision expressly exempts the authority from liability to pay the charge.
@ref s 5A(2), (3) (src:72-77)
GIVEN `passed before the commencement of section 5A` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the exemption would, apart from section 5A, apply to superannuation guarantee charge` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the law expressly exempts the authority from liability to pay the charge` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`a law exempts a Commonwealth authority from superannuation guarantee charge` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the exemption would, apart from section 5A, apply to superannuation guarantee charge`)
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF `passed before the commencement of section 5A`
         THEN JUST FALSE
         ELSE IF `the law expressly exempts the authority from liability to pay the charge`
              THEN NOTHING
              ELSE JUST FALSE

§ `Section 5B: the Fair Work Commission`

-- src:79 | (1) To avoid doubt, but subject to subsection (2), nothing in this Act (other than Part 3A) or in the Superannuation Guarantee Charge Act 1992 affects:
-- src:80 | (a) the jurisdiction, functions or powers of the Fair Work Commission; or
-- src:81 | (b) the operation of the Fair Work Act 2009, the Fair Work (Registered Organisations) Act 2009, or the Fair Work (Transitional Provisions and Consequential Amendments) Act 2009 in any other way.
@ref s 5B (src:79-81)
-- src:82 | (2) Subsection (1) does not apply to any express reference in the Fair Work Act 2009, the Fair Work (Registered Organisations) Act 2009, or the Fair Work (Transitional Provisions and Consequential Amendments) Act 2009 to this Act or to the Superannuation Guarantee Charge Act 1992.
@ref s 5B (src:82-82)
GIVEN `the provision is in Part 3A` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Fair Work legislation expressly refers to this Act or to the Superannuation Guarantee Charge Act 1992` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`this Act or the Superannuation Guarantee Charge Act 1992 affects the Fair Work Commission or the Fair Work legislation` MEANS
    IF `the provision is in Part 3A` OR `the Fair Work legislation expressly refers to this Act or to the Superannuation Guarantee Charge Act 1992`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST FALSE

§ `Section 5C: the Criminal Code`

-- src:83 | 5C Application of the Criminal Code
-- src:84 | Chapter 2 of the Criminal Code applies to all offences against this Act.
-- src:85 | Note: Chapter 2 of the Criminal Code sets out the general principles of criminal responsibility.
@ref s 5C (src:83-85)
GIVEN `the offence is an offence against this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Chapter 2 of the Criminal Code applies to the offence` MEANS
    IF `the offence is an offence against this Act` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING
